<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs steady in New York, Dow up 60 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs steady in New York, Dow up 60 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were steady in late New York trade while the Dow Industrials Index gained 60 points to 6,451.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$18 1/2	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28 7/8	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 1/4	 +0 5/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 3/4	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$12 3/4	  nil   *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$35 7/8	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  178 1/2 pence   -1 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  36		  -1</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  230		 -1</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  149		 +0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  142 1/2	   -2 1/2</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$2.98		-4</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.66		-1</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  untraded</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
